      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is an asymmetry in behavior when the change being queried (`changeData`) is itself ABANDONED:\n\n1. If `changeData` is abandoned and all other related changes are also abandoned (or it\u0027s a standalone change), `cds` is empty, and line 124 returns `Collections.emptyList()` immediately.\n2. If `changeData` is abandoned and there is at least one open related change, `cds` is non-empty, so execution reaches `reloadChangeIfStale` at line 130. `reloadChangeIfStale` (line 150) detects that `changeData` is missing from the index results (because `byProjectGroups` filtered it out) and reloads it from NoteDb, adding it back into the list. The abandoned queried change is then returned in the response despite `EXCLUDE_ABANDONED` being set.\n\nWe should clarify the desired contract when querying an abandoned change with `EXCLUDE_ABANDONED` (e.g. should the focal change always be included, or should it be omitted/empty?) and make sure the logic is consistent regardless of whether other related changes are open.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4cdb7bd065417323aeae5eb6c7b8d0124ee400ee",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
