        "id": 1030207
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T22:58:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If `thisPsd` has multiple parents (e.g. a merge commit) or an intermediate excluded merge commit had multiple parents that lead to the same ancestor `parentPsd`, `findParentsInGraph` (or iterating across parents) can yield the same `parentPsd` multiple times.\n\nBecause `parents` and `children` are `ListMultimap` instances, calling `put` will insert duplicate entries into `parents.get(thisPsd)` and `children.get(parentPsd)`. While `walkAncestors` uses a `LinkedHashSet`, `walkDescendentsImpl` will push redundant items into its pending deque. Consider deduplicating resolved parent entries before inserting, or using a `SetMultimap`.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4cdb7bd065417323aeae5eb6c7b8d0124ee400ee",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
